AI SYSTEMS  — key AI building blocks 
LLM as the brain for reasoning and text generation, 

RAG as added knowledge from documents and databases
AI agents as hands for taking actions with tools and memory.

MCP refers to the Model Context Protocol
an open standard launched by Anthropic in 2024 that acts as the "nervous system" 
standardized connections between AI models, external data sources, and tools for seamless integration

FUNDAMENTALS

LLM
  type        LargeLanguageModel
  role        Brain
  does        text generation by reasoning
  is          core intelligence
  input       prompt
  output      tokens / thought

RAG
  type        RetrievalAugmentedGeneration
  role        Brain + Books
  does        LLM + external knowledge
  uses        docs, databases, embeddings
  input       query + retrieved context
  output      grounded answer

AGENT
  type        AIAgent
  role        Brain + Hands
  does        takes actions
  uses        memory, tools, planning loop
  input       goal
  output      side effects / completed task

MCP
  type        ModelContextProtocol
  role        Nervous System
  does        connects everything
  is          standardized connection layer
  input       tools / resources / prompts
  output      shared context for models & agents

Understand these 4 → AI systems make a lot more sense.

